Q) Balanced Parentheses 
======================================================================
: Whenever I'm getting a closing bracket , I'm checking the last opening I saw, Is that was of my type
-> I should be able to see the last one , so which data structure - Stack 

code: class Solution {
    public boolean isValid(String s) {
        Stack<Character> st = new Stack<>();
        for(int i=0;i<s.length();i++)
        {
            char ch = s.charAt(i);
            if(ch=='(' || ch=='{' || ch=='[')
            {
                st.push(ch);
            }
            else if(ch==')')
            {
                if(!st.isEmpty() && st.peek()=='(') { st.pop(); }
                else {return false; }
            }
            else if(ch=='}')
            {
                if(!st.isEmpty() && st.peek()=='{') { st.pop(); }
                else{ return false; }
            }
            else{
                if(!st.isEmpty() && st.peek()=='[') { st.pop(); }
                else{ return false; }
            }
        }
        return st.isEmpty();
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N)
S.C. -> O(N)


Prefix,Infix,Postfix Conversions
===================================================

Operator: A symbol that performs an operation on one or more operands.
Operand: The values or variables on which the operator acts.
Example: In 5 + 3,
- + is the operator
- 5 and 3 are operands


Operator   Priority
^          3
* /        2
+ -        1  

Infix -> All the operators will be in between . Ex: (p+q)*(m-n)
Prefix -> All the operators will be pre(before) the operand . Ex: x+pq-mn
Postfix -> All the operators will be after the operand . Ex: pq+mn-*

